  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I've set up Harbor Desk, but I had to stop at its service keys. Those need you before it can go live.\n\n**Done:**\n- **Brief:** saved to `briefs/harbor_desk.md`.\n- **Settings:** written and checked. The workspace is Harbor Pilots, with owner@harbor.example as owner and ana@ and raj@ as members. Web search is on and the browser is off.\n- **Brand:** Harbor Desk in #0B6E4F.\n- **Custom code:** none needed; it uses the standard base as it is.\n\n**Blocked: keys.** Harbor Desk is missing six keys: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM`, `EXA_API_KEY` and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`. I tried to copy them from beta_app, which is already live, but this machine doesn't allow key values to be read out of Vercel. So each key has to be set by hand. Nothing was written to disk during the attempt.\n\n**Still to come:** after the keys, the next step is putting it online, which takes about 10 minutes. I'll ask for your yes before that. Then come the tests, which take about 30 minutes. For those you'll sign in once with a code from your email.\n\n**The first key: your Cloudflare account ID.** Harbor Desk uses Cloudflare to store the files people upload. This takes about 2 minutes.\n\n1. Open https://dash.cloudflare.com and sign in.\n2. Click your account name. The page that opens shows **Account ID** in the right-hand column. Click **Copy** next to it.\n3. Open a separate terminal window on the factory machine (for example a second SSH session), not this chat. Go to the factory folder and run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n4. Paste the ID when it asks and press Enter. What you paste stays hidden, and it only prints the key's name back. The value is saved only in Harbor Desk's Vercel settings, not in the factory's files or in this chat.\n\nTell me when it's done and I'll walk you through the next key.",
